1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:06,591
Fleet tools need credentials by name, and they need somewhere sensible to keep them.

2
00:00:06,591 --> 00:00:16,575
Lazarette Lite is the light answer: a browser window on the Windows Credential Manager you already have, with no new vault.

3
00:00:16,575 --> 00:00:20,651
This is a short run, using throwaway credentials only.

4
00:00:21,401 --> 00:00:24,933
Lazarette Lite is a browser window on the Windows Credential Manager.

5
00:00:24,933 --> 00:00:30,217
Double-click the launcher, and a small PowerShell server starts on this computer.

6
00:00:30,917 --> 00:00:35,890
The server listens on loopback only, on a port Windows picks.

7
00:00:35,890 --> 00:00:42,415
It answers only your own Windows user's processes, with a one-time launch token and a session cookie.

8
00:00:43,115 --> 00:00:49,573
The secrets themselves stay in Windows Credential Manager, as ordinary generic entries under a prefix.

9
00:00:49,573 --> 00:00:52,041
Lite ships no vault of its own.

10
00:00:52,741 --> 00:01:00,635
Fleet tools reach them through a loader that answers to the same command names as Lazarette: get a secret by service and user.

11
00:01:01,335 --> 00:01:07,649
What Lite does not do: custom fields, or Lazarette's key sharing with Fairlead.

12
00:01:07,649 --> 00:01:10,305
That stays with the full Lazarette.

13
00:01:11,005 --> 00:01:18,511
Safety: secrets stay hidden until you reveal them, delete asks first, and nothing outside its prefix is listed.

14
00:01:18,761 --> 00:01:21,798
First, add a credential in the browser.

15
00:01:21,798 --> 00:01:26,175
Service fleet-tools, user demo, and a secret I made up for this demo.

16
00:01:26,175 --> 00:01:30,564
The field masks it as it's typed, and none of it is a real password.

17
00:01:30,564 --> 00:01:31,364
Save.

18
00:01:31,503 --> 00:01:34,827
Saved, and it's already in Windows Credential Manager.

19
00:01:34,827 --> 00:01:37,512
The secret stays hidden until someone clicks Reveal.

20
00:01:37,512 --> 00:01:42,290
Here it is, blurred for the recording, because even a throwaway doesn't belong on screen.

21
00:01:42,882 --> 00:01:44,851
Now a Fleet tool asks for it by name.

22
00:01:44,851 --> 00:01:48,210
This is a short stand-in script, not a real tool.

23
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:53,892
It loads Lazarette the way the real ones do, and Start-LiteFleet points that loader at Lite.

24
00:01:54,592 --> 00:01:57,803
It gets the secret: fifteen characters.

25
00:01:57,803 --> 00:01:59,241
The value is never printed.

26
00:01:59,941 --> 00:02:01,494
Now a name Lite doesn't hold.

27
00:02:01,494 --> 00:02:03,600
It refuses with a plain error.

28
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:11,255
It never guesses, and it never hands back an empty password, so a tool fails early instead of running with nothing.

29
00:02:11,255 --> 00:02:12,625
Now the evidence trail.

30
00:02:12,625 --> 00:02:17,371
Get-LiteItemNames returns names only, never a secret.

31
00:02:17,371 --> 00:02:24,133
And this is the whole data store: an ordinary generic entry in Windows Credential Manager.

32
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:27,670
I also made a second throwaway entry outside Lite's prefix.

33
00:02:27,670 --> 00:02:31,797
Windows has it, you can see it here, and Lite's list never showed it.

34
00:02:31,797 --> 00:02:35,066
Lite only reads and writes entries under its own prefix.

35
00:02:35,766 --> 00:02:37,450
Cleanup belongs in the trail too.

36
00:02:37,450 --> 00:02:45,980
Delete asks you to confirm first, then the credential is removed from Windows Credential Manager, and the list is empty again.

37
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:48,867
Quit ends the session and the server stops.

38
00:02:49,170 --> 00:02:49,970
Nothing was left running.

39
00:02:50,177 --> 00:02:59,163
That is Lazarette Lite: named credentials for Fleet tools, from the Credential Manager you already have, with no new vault.

40
00:02:59,163 --> 00:03:05,885
Everything you saw ran for real on this PC, with throwaway credentials that are now deleted.

41
00:03:05,885 --> 00:03:09,099
The only stand-in was the short tool script.

42
00:03:09,099 --> 00:03:15,309
Custom fields and Lazarette's key sharing with Fairlead stay with the full Lazarette.

43
00:03:15,309 --> 00:03:16,113
Fair winds.
